# capability seated 20260906.140000 (REDS %493). The guard reads the SHIPPED side, so it needs a
# projection at `seed/` -- which is gitignored, built by `tools/s/sow.rish`, and therefore absent
# from every fresh clone. Rostered `tier lap` with no capability it went red on this tree's first
# cold pass after landing, and a red guard withholds the roster receipt, so `--scoped` refuses and
# every ship pays a FULL cold pass every lap: 778s measured here. The scan's own refusal is right
# (REDS %170) and the roster is where the environment fact belongs -- the same reading the operator
# card already gives an empty `vendor/`. Absence is announced by name rather than made silent.

# publish_template -- the one file this tree ships that a stranger RUNS against their own forge.
# publish-seed.sh is personal by law, so a newcomer inherits every room except a publisher;
# publish-seed.template.sh is that room. Two gates: no literal this field owns survives in it, and
# no stub lacks the GLOW_PROFILE field that answers it. Both fail QUIETLY otherwise -- a leftover
# remote reads as a working default until somebody pushes to a repository that is not theirs.
guard publish_template
path tools/p/publish_template_witness.rish
tier lap
