# Spool Cloth's name bound, seated 20260831.045858 -- the second half of one room's naming layer arriving
# in the shape museum. Tablecloth's four desks landed 20260829 and 20260830 and the last of them
# left the invitation on its own placard: pond/apps/spool_cloth.rye took the same wall in the same
# shape on the same day. The two modules are housemates rather than neighbours, since
# brushstroke/tablecloth.rye is a symlink into pond/apps/, so this is one room finishing its
# thought rather than a new vane arriving.
#
# The guard is shaped like its sibling: the scan reads the number the desk shows and the number the
# Rye publishes and compares them, holding no value of its own, so raising the bound honestly in
# both rooms walks free -- proven as a welcome beside the refusals rather than assumed.
#
# IT CARRIES TWO READINGS ITS SIBLING DOES NOT, and both were found by reading rather than by
# copying. First, this module reads max_name at TWO call sites: store_large refuses a long name
# with NameTooLong, and parse_manifest refuses a long field with BadManifest -- and the second
# guards an array's end rather than a policy, since a parsed name lands in a fixed [max_name]u8.
# They fire apart, so the control reads the survivor by name while its neighbour refuses. Second,
# the placard's SIXTH line is read by VALUE: PLACARD.md gives the nib its reason -- a pedestal
# displays a value AT a nib -- and every placard reading in the tree counts that keyword and stops,
# so across the 37 residents standing before this desk the stamp after it was compared to nothing.
# It is compared against spool_cloth_version now, so a module whose version moves while its desk
# keeps the elder nib reds here.
#
# A SECOND PEDESTAL JOINED IT 20260831.073652, and it carries a THIRD reading of its own kind.
# max_large_artifacts is shown beside the ceiling artifacts the shared bead store can pay for --
# four seats against a guarantee of two, measured on metal by the module's own selftest, since the
# catalog counts NAMES and the store counts BYTES. That guarantee is derived two levels deep out of
# mantra/beading.rye and mantra/spool.rye, so the scan RECOMPUTES it rather than reading a copy and
# reads the module's own derivation as a fact beside it. And the bound is the length of three fixed
# arrays in TWO modules: the third, KeyedLargeCatalog.owners in pond/apps/spool_keyed.rye, has no
# wall of its own and rides on store_large's through a `try` -- so the scan reads the bound where it
# CROSSES a module boundary, which no desk in this room had done before.
#
# Forty-seven control cases -- seven welcomes, forty refusals -- and thirteen named readings.
#
# `cadence` because the metal legs lower both desks through Glow and build them with the Zig
# toolchain, the same clock its Tablecloth sibling and the six Glow witnesses beside it keep.
# Re-measured on this pier 20260831.073652, GREEN before this row moved: 24s whole -- 17s of it the
# forty-seven-case control, the rest two Zig builds -- against a cold pass of 2,317s. The pure scan
# still runs in under a second, so a hand asking it by name pays almost nothing.

guard pond_spool_cloth_glow_tend
path tools/p/pond_spool_cloth_glow_tend_witness.rish
tier cadence
seated 20260831.045858

