# amphora -- the vessel family's eight witnesses, and not one of them stood on a clock. `amphora/`
# holds 7 tracked Rye modules of its own and 3,603 lines (corrected `20260906.063124`; the elder
# reading of 10 and 3,861 counted three symlinks into `tally/` and `comlink/` -- see *amphora, the
# crossing* at the foot of this file), and this roster named no guard over any of them. A lap that
# broke a seal, a stamp, or the chunk assembler would have shipped green, because nothing was
# listening -- and the chunk assembler stayed that way until the crossing rows landed. That is
# REDS %360's population exactly -- a guard that is never run guards nothing -- one family at a time.
#
# WHAT THE EIGHT PROVE, in the pairs they were written as. `pour` fills a vessel from the Cellar
# ring-1 season, seals the cargo, then stamps the canonical body; `carry` moves it to a far dock and
# proves the far bytes equal the near ones; `restore` scrubs cold and lands four files at the same
# parent; `grand_round` runs pour, carry and restore end to end and re-restores; `first_resident`
# pours a real counsel season and proves the out-home byte-equal. Each of the first three carries a
# NEGATIVE twin that plants at the wall it names -- a forged manifest line, a forked-season re-pour,
# an absent season, a tampered `seal_cargo`, a truncated vessel, a forged resin body, a torn chunk --
# and asserts the refusal by its own error name, with the standing vessel proven untouched after
# each. So the family already carries the half of the law a green reading can never show on its own:
# every one of these guards is proven able to red.
