seated 20260906.120137

# fold_shelf_link -- a link that kept the depth of the file it was folded out of (REDS %491, closing
# %474's booked loom). The card sits in `construction/`, so a link it writes as `](archive/X)` or
# `](../Y)` is correct there and broken the moment that text is folded onto `construction/archive/`.
# FOUR link guards read this tree and none reaches it, three of them for one shared reason: a fold
# shelf's basename carries a one-clock stamp, stamped means testimony, and testimony is where
# `tracked_link` reads past and `readme_reach` stops gating. The fold's own output wears the exact
# property that makes every guard let it go. Gating testimony is lawful here and nowhere else,
# because a depth-lost link was never correct in the file it sits in -- the fold broke it in the
# same act that created the file -- and it is told from a stale reference mechanically: it resolves
# under exactly ONE card-to-shelf correction where a stale one resolves under neither. Ambiguity is
# impossible by construction, since `archive/` and `../` are disjoint prefixes. 5s on metal; `lap`
# rather than `cadence` because the live front folds by hand on nearly every lap, and this fault
